      "question": "What are the red flags indicating impending airway compromise?",
      "my_answer": "Tripod positioning, drooling, stridor, muffled voice, refusal to speak, hypoxia (SpO2 92%), tachypnea, and anxiety are all red flags of severe airway obstruction.",
      "rationale": "These signs reflect increasing work of breathing and compensatory mechanisms. Drooling and refusal to speak indicate inability to manage secretions, a critical warning sign. Hypoxia in a child with stridor suggests significant airway narrowing."
    },
