      "my_answer": "Administer broad-spectrum intravenous antibiotics (e.g., ceftriaxone or cefotaxime) targeting Hib and other respiratory pathogens, and consider corticosteroids (though evidence is less strong in bacterial epiglottitis). Avoid any pharyngeal manipulation until airway is secure.",
